 SeaDate: 121200.1235<br>
 <br>
These are the continuing voyages of the USS(United SeaShip)Entertainer, its 5 month mission, to explore strange new ports, seek out new songs and new dance numbers, to boldly go where no Bard has gone before....<br>
<br>
(cue intro music)<br>
 <br>
(intro music/scene) Long view of a of big ocean going vessel at full sail...with a blue humanoid streak rushing by every time there is a crash in the music...<br>
(roll credits over intro music)<br>
 <br>
BARD TREK<br>
Servo Solderon as Captain Servo<br>
Reza Pinshon as Helmsman Ensign Reza<br>
Xeni Littlefury as Chief Medical Officer Xeni<br>
Faldaar Bedazzler as Science Officer Faldaar<br>
Widgiit Shinkicker as Chief Engineer Widgiit<br>
Scathach Eaglewolf as Communications Officer Scathach<br>
Nohmaad as Security Officer Nohmaad<br>
Dargaard Wolfmaster as Weapons Officer Dargaard<br>
Xaxo Bloodlylips as Ships Counselor<br>
Choka Bloodlytoes as Nurse Bloodlytoes<br>
Guest Starring Prestor Tigerheart as Yin <br>
Guest Starring Pentarum De'vir as Yang<br>
 <br>
(intro scene) Captain Servo is sitting in his command chair, stationed around him are his various officers doing normal ship's routine.<br>
 <br>
Servo:    Well crew, we are just about done with this cruise, we have been places that most people will never get to visit.  Seen more dance numbers then I can ever hope to remember!  We are just 11 days away from completing this mission, and I for one look forward to some shore leave!<br>
 <br>
Xeni:      I can use some myself, all this travelling all over the place and I have not had a chance to even stock up, even my medical cabinet is  looking bare! Damn it Servo, I'm a Doctor not a Barbarian!  We need to pull in and get some more medical supplies! <br>
 <br>
Servo:   Relax Xeni, we are making a stop at the beautiful Island of Hawaii tomorrow! You should be able to get everything you need and then some.  Faldaar, how long before actual arrival time?<br>
 <br>
Faldaar: Well Sir, considering the currents and the wind, I would say 11 hours, 12 mins, and 10 secs.<br>
 <br>
Servo: See Xeni, now just relax, what could possibly go wrong now? If you need me, I will be in my stateroom.  Faldaar you have the con.<br>
 <br>
(cue ominous sounding music)<br>
(cut to commercial)<br>
 Are you tired of being attacked by Giant Bee's and Wasp's?  Then get Bee-B-Gone and never be bothered by them again! Bee-B-Gone is a registered trademark of Norrath Industries.<br>
<br>
(come back from commercial)<br>
(scene of Servo reviewing some official looking documents at his desk)<br>
(cue RED ALERT sound)<br>
 <br>
(Faldaar over speakers) Red Alert, Red Alert, this is not a drill, I repeat, this is not a drill!  Captain Servo to the Bridge please...<br>
 <br>
Servo: What is it? What happened?<br>
 <br>
Faldaar: Sir, we seem to have ran into something, it appears to be a submarine of some sort.  I am attempting to find what class it is now...(computer noises and flashes)...ahh, here it is...it's an old Norrath Steamer, they were decommissioned in the late 3200's as being somewhat undependable.  How it managed to survive this long is an unknown.<br>
 <br>
Servo: Scathach, have you made contact with them yet?<br>
 <br>
Scathach: I'm trying to now sir, but they appear unable to receive our transmissions.<br>
 <br>
Servo: Well, we have a very old submarine in front of us, no<br>
communications, and it does not appear to be hostile, any suggestions?<br>
 <br>
Nohmaad: I would suggest a well armed crew attempt to beam onboard to investigate it, it might be old, but that does not mean it is not dangerous.<br>
 <br>
Faldaar: I agree with Nohmaad, we should investigate it, who knows how many scientific oddities might still be onboard.<br>
 <br>
Servo: Then it's settled, Nohmaad, Faldaar, Xeni, and Dargaard, your with me, Reza you have the con till we come back.<br>
 <br>
(Cut to teleporter room)<br>
 <br>
Widgiit: Ready for beam down Captain, I will have a tight beam lock on all your communication badges in case I need to pull an emergency recall.<br>
 <br>
Servo: Smart thinking Widgiit, 5 to beam down.<br>
 <br>
(cue sparkles and dissolve into submarine scene)<br>
 <br>
(inside of submarine, old pipes leaking and hissing, and rust everywhere)<br>
 <br>
Faldaar: Scanning for life signs sir, there appear to be two<br>
humanoids in that direction, very weak heartbeats as if they are in suspended animation.<br>
 <br>
Servo: Songs and spells set for stun gentlemen..<br>
 <br>
(cut to scene of two suspension cells holding two people inside)<br>
 <br>
Servo: Xeni, can you revive them?<br>
 <br>
(Xeni starts chanting and waving hands in front of cells, ice starts melting and the humans drop to the floor)<br>
 <br>
Xeni: That's all I can do for them, that really takes it out of you!  I am going to need a re-charge after this, you think I have unlimited mana or something!?!<br>
 <br>
Servo: Quite Xeni! Dargaard, check them for life signs and make sure they are safe...would not want any sudden spells going off in here, who knows what might happen.<br>
 <br>
Dargaard:  They appear to be fine Sir, although a bit worse for wear.  Being frozen for however long these two have been is not good for the body!<br>
 <br>
Servo: Xeni, can you take care of them in sickbay? Perhaps bring them back to the conscious world maybe?<br>
 <br>
Xeni: I can try Servo, but I am not making any promises, after all, I am a cleric, not a witch doctor!<br>
 <br>
Servo: Entertainer, beam Xeni and his two patients to sickbay.<br>
(background noise of transporter effect) Well gentleman, shall we investigate further, there is no telling what we may find here.  Dargaard you and Nohmaad check that aisle, Faldaar and I shall check this aisle.<br>
 <br>
(The group splits up, Servo is seen standing and counting in place)<br>
 <br>
Servo: 1...2...3...4...5...6...7...(noise of person dropping into<br>
something hot, and screaming) Well, it would appear Dargaard is getting better, he made it to 7 before he found something to fall into and die in.  Entertainer, Beam the remains of Dargaard to Sickbay so Xeni can resurrect him again.  Nohmaad,  you going to be ok on your own?  <br>
 <br>
Nohmaad: (tiny voice over combadge) I will be Sir, but I must protest you always sending me out with him, he manages to die every time we split up!<br>
 <br>
(cut to commercial)<br>
Need to be somewhere fast? Then hire Druid Airlines, guaranteed to get you there faster then you can say &quot;FIZBANG!&quot; Druid Airlines, we love to travel, and it shows!<br>
(come back from commercial)<br>
 <br>
(scene of &quot;the gang&quot; in the ready room discussing the two persons in sickbay)<br>
 <br>
Servo: Let's go over this again, based on what we found onboard their vessel, they are renegades from some city called Fiorina Vie.  They were being hunted down because they were two &quot;enemies&quot; actually working together as a team, complete opposites of each other.  What makes no sense is why, what were these two doing together if they are such mortal enemies as the data says?  Any guesses?<br>
 <br>
Faldaar: It's quite possible Sir that they were perhaps working on a mutual goal, and the necessity of the situation required them to join forces in order to accomplish this deed.  I have heard of several races doing this in order to accomplish something, but what will usually happen is once the goal is achieved, they go right back to the way they were, hating each other.<br>
 <br>
Nohmaad: I say we let them talk and tell us their story, we may be able to figure out more of what happened then sitting here talking about it, but I do like these big get togethers where we stand around and discuss things for hours before we actually do something about it.  Makes the day go by so much quicker!<br>
 <br>
Widgiit: To be honest with you Sir, I have seen much in my time onboard, and this is just another one of them circumstances where we have to puzzle out some sort of mystery, then solve it by randomly killing someone, then working it all out before dinnertime, same plot over and<br>
over...I would rather get my hands on that submarine out there!  I can think of several new improvements I could add to the Entertainer with the things they have......<br>
 <br>
(smirks and grins around the table from &quot;the gang&quot;)<br>
 <br>
Reza: You already know my answer Captain, let them tell us their stories and we can take it from there.<br>
 <br>
Xaxo: As the ship's counselor, I would recommend that we at least quarantine them in sickbay, since we have no idea of what sort of germs or diseases they may be carrying.<br>
 <br>
(cut to scene of Xeni and Choka escorting the &quot;two&quot; into the Ready Room)<br>
 <br>
Xeni: Well guess no more, here they are, but don't be keeping them up all day, they are still recovering from the effects of the suspension chamber!<br>
 <br>
Servo: Gentlemen I am Captain Servo, and may I welcome you aboard the USS Entertainer, this is my crew, that is Faldaar my Science Officer, there is Widgiit my Chief Engineer, Reza my Second in Command, Xaxo the Ship's Counselor, Nohmaad my Security Chief, and you have already met Xeni<br>
and Choka my Medical Staff.  Have you been comfortable, can I get you something to eat, drink?  Have a seat, we have some questions we would like to ask  of you, and I am sure you have yours as well to ask.<br>
 <br>
(insert cliff hanger message here)<br>
TO BE CONTINUED NEXT WEEK...<br>
(fade out, cue closing music and credits)<br>
<br>
<br>
